-- title:
--   Minimality over (q) and distinctness of the two generic points
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $q$ with $N_0 \neq 0$ and $q$ prime, and assume $q \nmid N_0$; let $\mathfrak{P}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN` for the scheme $X(N_0,q)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the base ring `DRLevel.R q`, with structure morphism `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` (the Igusa morphism at level $N_0 q$). Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ (with decidable equality) and $\mathrm{to}\kappa :$ `DRLevel.R q` $\to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism, and assume the scheme `DRLevel.fibre0 toκ`, the fibre product of `toBase0 N₀ q` with $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$, is integral, so that it has a generic point $\eta$. For $i \in \{0,1\}$ write $p_i$ for the image of $\eta$ under the morphism `𝔓.comp κ toκ i` from `DRLevel.fibre0 toκ` to the base change of `toBase N₀ q` along $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$, followed by the first projection of that pullback, so $p_i$ is a point of $X(N_0,q)$. The assertion is threefold: (1) if $p_i$ equals the image under `IgusaScheme.ιFin (N₀ * q) q` of a prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q` (the chart subalgebra attached to $j$ at level $N_0q$), then $\mathfrak{q}$ is a minimal prime over the ideal generated by $q$ in that algebra; (2) the same with `ιInf` and the chart algebra `chartAlgInf (N₀ * q) q` attached to $j^{-1}$; and (3) $p_0 \neq p_1$.
--
--   This records the two labelled components of the characteristic-$q$ fibre of the Igusa-type model as distinct irreducible components of the special fibre: each generic point, when it lies in one of the two standard charts, corresponds to a minimal prime over $(q)$, and the two points are distinct. It feeds the Néron-component analysis of the model, in particular the statements identifying the chart prime under the first generic point and the vanishing properties of the associated local data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel_mem_minimalPrimes_of_fst_comp_genericPoint_eq_and_fst_comp_ne.lean

